                <pb facs="0701" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.6363/174</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-09"><hi rendition="#italic">June 9,
                            1924</hi></date>.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d528-f1"/></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 618</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 15 of May 24th, 6 P.M. and No. 16 of May 31, 7 P.M.,<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d528-f2"/> and to the Legation’s telegram No. 18 of May 27th, 6
                    P.M., No. 19 of May 30th, 11 A.M. and No. 21 of June 3rd, 4 P.M., concerning the
                    proposed mining law, I have the honor to transmit herewith copies of a note
                    addressed by the Legation on June 6th to the Rumanian Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs pointing out a second time certain of the objectionable clauses of the
                    law in question.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Peter A. Jay</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d528-a1.xml" xpointer="d528-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
